 # Release workflow
 
+## Proposed 0.17.0, not yet published
+
+Public npm `latest` was verified as `0.16.0` on 2026-11-01. Repository metadata still
+reported `0.15.1`; the older preparation notes below are historical and do not establish
+registry state. This additive `0.17.0` candidate does not replace any immutable version.
+
+The candidate includes the OpenRouter reasoning-replay binding fix from PR #49, the
+opt-in generic request projection and sanitized error details from PR #50, and detached
+projection input from PR #51. Its merged source is `3c8ab12a1cd52f384f4953eb69f8e80553a49bc2`,
+tree `46d025d8224acdc3bd3d15dcefd7a975b1f585bf`. The version/docs preparation is local-only;
+its separate release record must identify the exact metadata commit, final archive,
+independent checks and merged-source CI before account-holder publication.
+Authentication, account storage, consent UI and approval modes remain host-owned; core
+neither signs users in nor adopts the separate CLI changes. Runtime dependencies remain
+unchanged. Live providers and OAuth login have not been exercised.
+
+The account holder publishes only the exact final independently reviewed archive after
+source, package and clean installed-consumer checks. Do not publish this draft source or
+update host pins before the real release and registry-byte verification.
+
